course: dictionary
lesson: 6539
title: The neutron, a particle with no charge
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Atoms are very tiny, but they are not solid blobs: they are made of smaller parts. «An atom is made of smaller parts: protons and neutrons in a tiny middle called the nucleus, and electrons around it.» The clue is the word parts: a neutron is one of the smaller parts.
explain: Look at the words around neutron. Protons and neutrons sit together in the nucleus, the tiny middle of the atom. Since neutrons are found there, you can work out that a neutron is one of the particles in the centre. Check it: does «one of the tiny particles in the centre of an atom» fit the sentence? It does.
explain: The word neutral is the clue to the charge. A neutron is neutral, so it has no electric charge: it is neither positive nor negative. Protons are positive and electrons are negative, so neutrons are the part with no sign.
explain: Scientists use the same word in different places. «A collapsed core can become a neutron star» tells you that neutron star is the name of a type of star, not a particle. Context shows you which meaning is in use.
fact: A neutron is one of the tiny particles in the nucleus, the centre of an atom.
fact: A neutron has no electric charge: it is neutral.
fact: Protons are positive, electrons are negative, and neutrons are neutral.
fact: A «neutron star» is the very small, very heavy core left after some huge stars explode.
fact: Neutrons are important in nuclear power stations, where they split atoms.
exercise: Where are neutrons found in an atom? | *In the nucleus, the tiny middle | Around the outside in a cloud | Only in the Sun | Inside the electrons
exercise: What does neutral tell you about a neutron? | It is bigger than a proton | It has a negative charge | *It has no electric charge | It has a positive charge
exercise: «A collapsed core can become a neutron star.» What is a neutron star? | A star that is very close to the Earth | A large, cool planet | A particle with a big positive charge | *A very small, very heavy star left after a huge star explodes
test: What is the middle of an atom called? | Star | Pulsar | *Nucleus | Electron
test: Protons are positive and electrons are negative. What are neutrons? | Positive | Negative | Radio beams | *Neutral, with no charge
exam: In «protons and neutrons in a tiny middle called the nucleus», what does neutron mean? | A beam of radio waves | A large star that explodes | A negative particle that moves around the nucleus | *A tiny particle in the nucleus with no electric charge
